        "text": "Emergency admission for bacterial pneurnonia.\nKnown history of severe Penicillln allergy (confirmed anaphylaxis).\nTreated with Levofloxacin 500 mg IV OD (avoiding beta-lactams due to allergy).\nDuring hospitalization, patient reported experiencing facial swelling and mild urticaria\napproximately 2 hours after receiving a dose of a combination medication that was later\nfound to contain amoxicillin (a penicillin-class antibiotic).\nThe reaction was managed with antihistamines and the medication was discontinued\nimmediately.\nPossible hypersensitivity reaction following inadvertent exposure to an amoxicillin-\ncontaining medication.\nThis possible allergy-related finding requires further evaluation.\nReported reaction - NOT CONFIRMED as a new allergy.\nRecommend allergy/immunology consultation for formal assessment.\n[STAMP: APEX CLINICAL CENTRE - EMERGENCY DEPT - COPY]",
